WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.421 --> 00:00:16.332
When Heidi finished playing under the fir trees, she found Grandfather sitting on his chair facing the valley.

2
00:00:16.733 --> 00:00:21.497
She went straight up to the old man, put out her hand, and said, "Good evening, Grandfather."

3
00:00:22.097 --> 00:00:25.840
It didn't bother her that Grandfather was rude to Detie, and even a little to her.

4
00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:28.703
"What do you want?"

5
00:00:29.243 --> 00:00:29.784
he asked.

6
00:00:30.272 --> 00:00:33.173
"I want to see inside the house," said Heidi.

7
00:00:33.193 --> 00:00:34.714
"Come, then!"

8
00:00:35.114 --> 00:00:36.955
Grandfather rose and stepped to the door.

9
00:00:36.975 --> 00:00:39.216
"Bring your bundle of clothes with you."

10
00:00:39.236 --> 00:00:43.237
"I don't want them anymore," Heidi said.

11
00:00:43.257 --> 00:00:46.098
"And why don't you want them?"

12
00:00:46.699 --> 00:00:47.179
he asked.

13
00:00:47.199 --> 00:00:50.800
"Because I want to run on the mountain like the goats."

14
00:00:51.461 --> 00:00:53.261
The old man turned and looked at Heidi.

15
00:00:53.822 --> 00:00:56.363
Her eyes seemed to sparkle with happy anticipation.

16
00:00:56.383 --> 00:01:01.293
"She is definitely intelligent," he thought to himself.

17
00:01:01.313 --> 00:01:08.058
"Well, you can go about like the goats if you want to," said Grandfather, "but bring your things

18
00:01:08.158 --> 00:01:08.759
in anyway.

19
00:01:09.299 --> 00:01:10.881
We must put them in the cupboard."

20
00:01:12.082 --> 00:01:13.463
Heidi did as she was told.

21
00:01:13.963 --> 00:01:15.264
Inside the hut was one room.

22
00:01:16.005 --> 00:01:20.769
There was a small table and a chair on one side, and Grandfather's bed was in a corner.

23
00:01:21.389 --> 00:01:23.451
There was also a large fireplace.

24
00:01:24.051 --> 00:01:25.453
Next to the bed was the cupboard.

25
00:01:26.053 --> 00:01:29.376
They put her belongings inside, right next to Grandfather's things.

26
00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:32.761
Heidi then looked carefully around the room.

27
00:01:32.781 --> 00:01:34.982
"Where am I going to sleep?"

28
00:01:35.482 --> 00:01:36.002
she asked.

29
00:01:36.022 --> 00:01:38.903
"Wherever you like," he answered.

30
00:01:39.504 --> 00:01:40.584
Heidi was delighted.

31
00:01:41.224 --> 00:01:45.266
After examining all the corners of the room, she saw a short ladder and climbed it.

32
00:01:47.367 --> 00:01:48.967
At the top was the hayloft.

33
00:01:49.548 --> 00:01:52.129
In it was a large heap of fresh, sweet-smelling hay.

34
00:01:52.569 --> 00:01:55.470
Through a round hole in the wall she could see right down the valley.

35
00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:59.091
"I want to sleep up here, Grandfather," she told him.

36
00:01:59.111 --> 00:02:00.572
"It is so lovely."

37
00:02:02.849 --> 00:02:07.613
They busily arranged the hay into a soft bed and found a sheet and a warm blanket.

38
00:02:08.233 --> 00:02:12.477
Now Heidi could lie in her bed and fall asleep looking down on the beautiful valley below.

39
00:02:13.978 --> 00:02:16.100
After all their work, it was time to eat.

40
00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:18.161
Heidi quickly found the bowls.

41
00:02:18.181 --> 00:02:22.605
"Good, I see you know how to set the table," said Grandfather.

42
00:02:23.166 --> 00:02:27.049
He put out the food, and they ate a delicious meal of cheese, bread, and milk.

43
00:02:27.789 --> 00:02:30.051
Heidi had never tasted anything so wonderful.

44
00:02:30.972 --> 00:02:32.433
"Was the milk good?"

45
00:02:32.913 --> 00:02:33.853
asked Grandfather.

46
00:02:33.873 --> 00:02:38.475
"It's the best milk I've ever had," said Heidi.

47
00:02:38.495 --> 00:02:40.956
"Then you must have some more."

48
00:02:41.437 --> 00:02:43.357
Grandfather poured her another big cup.

49
00:02:44.078 --> 00:02:45.638
Suddenly, they heard a sharp whistle.

50
00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:49.620
They went outside and watched as goats came springing down the mountain.

51
00:02:51.001 --> 00:02:53.702
In their midst was Peter, the twelve-year-old goatherd.

52
00:02:54.582 --> 00:02:58.704
Peter lived with his old, blind grandmother a little further down the mountain.

53
00:02:59.516 --> 00:03:02.857
As Peter neared Grandfather's hut, the goats stood still.

54
00:03:03.397 --> 00:03:05.958
Two of them ran forward to where Grandfather was standing.

55
00:03:05.978 --> 00:03:08.899
"Are they yours, Grandfather?"

56
00:03:09.259 --> 00:03:10.599
Heidi asked excitedly.

57
00:03:10.619 --> 00:03:17.081
"Yes, yes, the white one is named Daisy, and the brown one, Dusky," Grandfather said.

58
00:03:18.661 --> 00:03:23.182
Heidi watched as he milked the white goat and then settled them both in their shed for the

59
00:03:23.222 --> 00:03:26.823
night. Next, it was Heidi's turn to settle down for the night.

60
00:03:27.343 --> 00:03:29.044
She climbed up to her bed of straw.

61
00:03:29.789 --> 00:03:34.611
Soon, she was sleeping as sweetly and soundly as any young princess on a silk bed.
